@Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5205

### Root check
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/
Accept: text/plain

### ============================================================
### 1. Make a new registration — POST /api/registrations
### ============================================================

### Case 01: Valid Competitor, partly paid (201 Created)
# @name createCompetitor
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1001",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 02: Valid Exhibitor, not paid (201 Created)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1002",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 0
}

### Case 03: Valid VIP, fully paid (201 Created)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1003",
  "registrationType": "VIP",
  "amountPaid": 5000
}

### Case 05: Client tries to set server-only fields (201 Created, extra fields ignored)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1005",
  "registrationType": "VIP",
  "amountPaid": 0,
  "registrationFee": 1,
  "status": "Confirmed",
  "registrationNumber": "HACK-1"
}

### Case 06: All text fields empty (400 Bad Request)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "",
  "contactNumber": "",
  "email": "",
  "address": "",
  "carMakeModel": "",
  "plateNumber": "",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 07: Invalid contact number (400 Bad Request)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "12345",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1007",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 08: Invalid email (400 Bad Request)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan-at-example",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1008",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 09: Paid more than the fee (400 Bad Request)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1009",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 2000
}

### Case 10: Negative amount paid (400 Bad Request)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1010",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": -100
}

### Case 11: Unknown registration type (400 Bad Request)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1011",
  "registrationType": "Sponsor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 12: Text longer than allowed - participantName 151 chars (400 Bad Request)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1012",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 13: Duplicate plate number (409 Conflict)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1001",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### ============================================================
### 2. Show all registrations — GET /api/registrations
### ============================================================

### Case 14 & 15: Default list, newest first (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Accept: application/json

### Case 16: Second page, custom size (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=2&pageSize=5
Accept: application/json

### Case 17: Page past the end (200 OK, empty items)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=999
Accept: application/json

### Case 18: Invalid page (400 Bad Request)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?page=0
Accept: application/json

### Case 19: Page size too large (400 Bad Request)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?pageSize=100
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================
### 3. Find by type, status and participant name
### ============================================================

### Case 20: Find by type (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?type=VIP
Accept: application/json

### Case 21: Find by status (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?status=Confirmed
Accept: application/json

### Case 22: Find by participant name lowercase (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=juan
Accept: application/json

### Case 23: Find by participant name uppercase (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=JUAN
Accept: application/json

### Case 24: Partial name match (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=dela
Accept: application/json

### Case 25: Combined filters (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?type=Competitor&status=Pending&participantName=juan
Accept: application/json

### Case 26: No matches (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?participantName=zzzzzz
Accept: application/json

### Case 27: Invalid type (400 Bad Request)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?type=Sponsor
Accept: application/json

### Case 28: Invalid status (400 Bad Request)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?status=Done
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================
### 4. Find registration by ID — GET /api/registrations/{id}
### ============================================================

### Case 29: Existing ID from Case 01 (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/{{createCompetitor.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### Case 30: ID that doesn't exist (404 Not Found)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Accept: application/json

### Case 31: Not a valid GUID (404 Not Found)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/abc
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================
### 5. KPI summary — GET /api/registrations/summary
### ============================================================

### Case 32-36 & 38: Summary KPI totals (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json

### Case 37: Create another Exhibitor to verify summary updates (201 Created)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1037",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 500
}

### Verify summary after Case 37 (200 OK)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/registrations/summary
Accept: application/json
